# Dispatcher

When ingesting, granting, revoking, or answering from Cognee, read both files and follow them:

- `.cursor/skills/dispatcher/RULES.md` — what must stay true (the named dataset, sync sets, hard stops)
- `.cursor/skills/dispatcher/SKILL.md` — the procedure

Cognee is the only memory store. The organization and the dataset are named before ingestion. Dispatcher does not read the file to choose the dataset, and it does not read the file to check that name. `remember()` stores the file in the named dataset and adds to that graph when the dataset already exists. A dataset that already holds another organization is not reused. There is no director and no superuser. A person can read the datasets named for them on the access map. The question runs as that person, not as the owner. A closed dataset is removed and the open datasets are still searched. A dataset the question names and the person cannot read is answered `You do not have access.` Open datasets that do not answer the question are answered `That is not in the information you can access.` The answer keeps only the sentences the question asks for, from one dataset or from several, and it is not stored. An employee number in the question is an exact lookup on that record, on the datasets that person can read. The same entity id in two graphs is not an edge. If these two files disagree, RULES.md wins.
